//RS /// c109 Phase 22: is a method-call collection iteration (`loop x in <coll>` where
//RS /// `<coll>` is an `Expr::MethodCall`) in-subset? Mirrors `emit_for_in`'s
//RS /// `Expr::MethodCall` branches (Source/Codegen/Statement.rs):
//RS ///  - `.chars()` — char iteration; only the *receiver* (a string) is emitted, so it
//RS ///    must be in-subset.
//RS ///  - `.lines()` — streaming `BufRead::lines`; the receiver is a `FileReader`/
//RS ///    `StdinHandle` (or inline `io.stdin()`), again emitted on its own, so it must be
//RS ///    in-subset. (Both lines shapes route here; the FileReader-vs-stdin split is
//RS ///    resolved at lowering off `tir_recv_jet_ty`/the inline-`stdin` shape.)
//RS ///  - any other method — the `.iter().cloned()` default, which emits the WHOLE method
//RS ///    call as the collection value, so the whole call must be in-subset (e.g. a
//RS ///    Phase-9 `.split(…)` builtin returns a `[String]` value).
